        "section_width": "full_width",
        "reset_spacing": true,
        "reveal": false,
        "subheading_text": "<p>Making content is a small business with a lot of moving parts. Forty ideas, three scripts on the go, a calendar for four platforms and a sponsor who wants a draft by Thursday.</p><p>Most of us run it from a notes app, a few documents and an inbox. That works for the first month. Then an upload slips because the script was in the wrong folder.</p><p>Creator OS is the system we wished we had:</p><ul><li>every idea on one board, scored and moved along</li><li>a script page with the hook first</li><li>one calendar for every platform</li><li>sponsors with the fee, the deliverable and the due date</li><li>the numbers for each post, logged once a week</li></ul><p>It is plain on purpose. Seven pages you will open every week and a review that takes twenty minutes on a Friday.</p><p>New to Notion? The walkthrough video covers everything you need.</p>",
        "content_alignment": "left",
